  "content": {
    "id": "p46-q13",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A business has five times as many junior workers as it does senior workers.\n\nIf the weekly wage for a senior is $\\$800$ and for a junior is $\\$600$, find how many of each are employed if the total weekly wage bill is $\\$57000$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "15 senior workers and 75 junior workers.",
      "worked": "Let $s$ be the number of senior workers and $j$ be the number of junior workers.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nj &= 5s &&\\text{(1)}\\\\\n800s + 600j &= 57000 &&\\text{(2)}\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute (1) into (2).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n800s + 600(5s) &= 57000\\\\\n800s + 3000s &= 57000\\\\\n3800s &= 57000\\\\\ns &= 15\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $s=15$ into (1).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nj &= 5(15)\\\\\nj &= 75\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe business employs 15 senior workers and 75 junior workers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
